m 5','Chapter 2: Matrices','verified',0.95,1,4,'Chapter 2: Matrices','Form 5','SPM_2021_Q14_S1',1,'',3.00,'marking_scheme',1),(1089,49,'15','a','','','Structured','Equations and Inequalities','Linear Inequalities','Form 4','Chapter 6: Linear Inequalities in Two Variables','[\"A roller coaster in a theme park has 12 rows of seats. There are 3 seats in each row. The rule of riding the roller coaster is that a child must be accompanied by at least one adult.\", \"Using x to represent the number of children and y to represent the number of adults, write two linear inequalities other than x > 0 and y > 0 to represent the given situation, such that the number of passengers is at most maximum.\"]','[\"Sebuah \'roller coaster\' di sebuah taman tema mempunyai 12 baris tempat duduk. Terdapat 3 tempat duduk bagi setiap baris. Peraturan menaiki \'roller coaster\' itu ialah seorang kanak-kanak mesti ditemani oleh sekurang-kurangnya seorang dewasa.\", \"Menggunakan x untuk mewakili bilangan kanak-kanak dan y untuk mewakili bilangan dewasa, tulis dua ketaksamaan linear selain x > 0 dan y > 0 bagi mewakili situasi yang diberi, dengan keadaan bilangan penumpang adalah selebih-lebihnya maksimum.\"]','[\"text_0\", \"text_1\"]','[]','[\"x > 0\", \"y > 0\"]','[\"x\", \"y\"]','{\"rows\": 12, \"seats_per_row\": 3}','{}','{\"max_passengers\": 36, \"child_accompanied_by_adult\": true}','[]','Write two linear inequalities other than x > 0 and y > 0 to represent the situation with maximum passengers.',0,'','Easy',2,'','{\"form\": \"Form 4\", \"part\": \"a\", \"marks\": 2.0, \"topic\": \"Equations and Inequalities\", \"target\": \"Write two linear inequalities other than x > 0 and y > 0 to represent the situation with maximum passengers.\", \"chapter\": \"Chapter 6: Linear Inequalities in Two Variables\", \"options\": [], \"subpart\": \"\", \"_page_no\": 18, \"group_id\": \"SPM_2021_Q15\", \"sequence\": [\"text_0\", \"text_1\"], \"subtopic\": \"Linear Inequalities\", \"equations\": [], \"varia