9/mathsy/question_diagrams/cuispa9dxhq9jugeqetm.jpg','2026-05-11 14:21:47','Selangor_2023_Q15','Foundation','Foundation: Mensuration','foundation_verified',0.85,3,5,'Foundation: Mensuration','Foundation','Selangor_2023_Q15_S2',2,'Selangor_2023_Q15_S1',4.00,'marking_scheme',1),(1141,51,'16','b','i','','Structured','Equations and Inequalities','Linear Inequalities','Form 4','Chapter 6: Linear Inequalities in Two Variables','[\"Encik Emir needs to select at most 20 customers every day for the lucky draw, while the number of female customers must be at least twice the number of male customers.\", \"Using x to represent the number of female customers and y to represent the number of male customers, write two linear inequalities other than x ≥ 0 and y ≥ 0 that represent the conditions for selecting the winner of the lucky draw.\"]','[\"Encik Emir perlu memilih selebih-lebihnya 20 orang pelanggan setiap hari bagi cabutan bertuah, manakala bilangan pelanggan perempuan perlu sekurang-kurangnya dua kali bilangan pelanggan lelaki.\", \"Menggunakan x untuk mewakili bilangan pelanggan perempuan dan y untuk mewakili bilangan pelanggan lelaki, tulis dua ketaksamaan linear selain x ≥ 0 dan y ≥ 0 yang mewakili syarat pemilihan pemenang cabutan bertuah.\"]','[\"text_0\", \"text_1\"]','[]','[\"x ≥ 0\", \"y ≥ 0\"]','[\"x\", \"y\"]','{\"max_customers\": 20, \"female_customers_min_twice_male_customers\": true}','{}','{}','[]','Write two linear inequalities other than x ≥ 0 and y ≥ 0 that represent the conditions for selecting the winner of the lucky draw.',0,'','Easy',2,'','{\"form\": \"Form 4\", \"part\": \"b\", \"marks\": 2.0, \"topic\": \"Equations and Inequalities\", \"target\": \"Write two linear inequalities other than x ≥ 0 and y ≥ 0 that represent the conditions for selecting the winner of the lucky draw.\", \"chapter\": \"Chapter 6: Linear Inequalities in Two Variables\", \"options\": [], \"subpart\": \"i\", \"_page_no\": 36, \"group_id\": \"Selangor_2023_Q16\", \"sequence\": [\